---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/for';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'for');
const desc = description(site, 'for');
const routes = [
  ['fashion', 'Fashion', 'Exact-size restocks, drops, exchanges and seasonal returns.'],
  ['beauty', 'Beauty', 'Usage education, shade preferences and routine replenishment.'],
  ['supplements', 'Supplements', 'Product-approved education, consumption assumptions and subscription state.'],
  ['jewelry', 'Jewelry', 'Gift privacy, personalization deadlines, sizing and custom commissions.'],
  ['home-goods', 'Home goods', 'Room preferences, compatible accessories and split deliveries.'],
  ['food-and-beverage', 'Food and beverage', 'Supply estimates, perishability, gifts and shipping cutoffs.'],
  ['pet-products', 'Pet products', 'Species and life-stage relevance, pack usage and subscription changes.'],
  ['digital-products', 'Digital products', 'Access delivery, first use, licenses and renewal ownership.'],
  ['print-on-demand', 'Print on demand', 'Design relevance, production expectations and contribution after fulfillment.'],
  ['high-aov', 'High-AOV', 'Specification research, consultation handoffs, quotes and installation.'],
  ['subscription-boxes', 'Subscription boxes', 'Box previews, skips, billing state and cancellation handling.'],
  ['b2b-wholesale', 'B2B wholesale', 'Account approval, reorder context and sales-rep coordination.'],
];
const faqs = [
  { question: 'Which guide should I read first?', answer: 'Choose the guide for the email job that currently causes the most operational difficulty. A beauty subscription business may need both beauty and subscription-box guidance.' },
  { question: 'Does store type determine the winning platform?', answer: 'No. It helps identify required data, message timing and failure cases. Demonstrate those cases with your actual systems before selecting a supplier.' },
  { question: 'How many platforms should I shortlist?', answer: 'Include only candidates that can meet the essential workflow and ownership requirements. There is no fixed number that makes a shortlist serious.' },
  { question: 'When should I migrate?', answer: 'First identify a specific limitation and confirm that a candidate resolves it. Plan consent, suppressions, queued messages, event cutover and rollback before changing platforms.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <h1 class="hero-title">Shopify email tools by store type</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Start with what the customer needs to do next. A gift deadline, a furniture delivery and a digital access problem require different data and different owners. Use this index to find that workflow before comparing software.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container py-12">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl">Find your catalog and operating model</h2>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {routes.map(([slug, name, job]) => <a class="card" href={`/for/${slug}`}><h3 class="text-xl font-bold">{name}</h3><p class="mt-3">{job}</p></a>)}
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Resolve overlaps before adding more flows</h2>
    <p>A beauty subscription seller needs usage education from the beauty guide and skip-state handling from the boxes guide. An upcoming recurring shipment should affect a reorder reminder. A jewelry seller with custom appointments needs gift deadlines plus the quote handoff in the high-AOV guide. An active commission should pause generic cart recovery.</p>
    <p>Write one precedence rule for each overlap and name its owner. Start with service issues and purchase state, then decide which promotional message remains relevant. Reading two guides should produce one coherent customer journey, not two independent sequences competing for the same inbox.</p>
    <h2>Turn the guide into a supplier brief</h2>
    <p>List the essential event, its system of record, the customer identifier, required fields, expected delay and fallback when it is missing. For furniture this may be an item-level delivery state; for digital products, an access or first-use event from the delivery provider. Shopify checkout data alone does not prove that the external event reaches an email platform.</p>
    <p>Ask each candidate to demonstrate the hardest case using a staff record. Sequenzy can be included alongside other candidates; this index assigns no default winner. Compare evidence of the requested integration, operator effort, message controls and a quote for your actual audience and sending pattern. Popup capture, SMS, CRM and lifecycle email may have separate owners; avoid paying for overlapping jobs without a reason.</p>
    <h2>Use a staged implementation, with an exit condition</h2>
    <p>Inventory existing messages and consent records first. Confirm service-message ownership, then introduce the highest-priority missing workflow. Proposed acceptance cases should include purchase during a queued sequence, an unsubscribe, missing data and a changed customer preference. Add the next flow only when the current one has clear entry, pause and exit behavior.</p>
    <p>A migration needs additional checks for historical suppressions, event duplication and queued sends in the old platform. Set a rollback decision and owner before cutover. Do not interpret a larger attributed revenue number after migration as proof of improvement without checking attribution windows, returns and a comparable audience.</p>
    <h2>Read the next resource for the next decision</h2>
    <p>Use the <a class="link" href="/apps">tool catalog</a> to locate supplier profiles, the <a class="link" href="/compare">comparison hub</a> for finalists and <a class="link" href="/use-cases">use-case guides</a> for individual flows. Check current supplier documentation and obtain a scoped demonstration where a profile makes a capability claim. These guides do not establish merchant test results or a sitewide ranking.</p>
    <p>Shopify documents its service notifications for orders, shipping, refunds, exchanges and accounts in <a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/fulfillment/setup/notifications">Store notifications</a>, checked 24 November 2026. Use that as a starting boundary for service ownership, not as proof that an external email tool receives every event.</p>
  </div></section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Store-type guide FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
